Revision history for EV-Telegram-TDLib

0.04    2026-09-09
        SECURITY: an unusable TDLIB_LOG_VERBOSITY (empty or non-numeric)
        left TDLib logging at its own default level instead of the
        quiet one this module sets. TDLib's log can carry the requests
        that hold your api_hash and bot token, so treat stderr from any
        run that set the variable as sensitive. It now falls back to 1.
        INCOMPATIBLE: database_encryption_key is now encoded correctly.
        0.03 sent it raw, so most passphrases made TDLib refuse the
        request and kill login, while one shaped like base64 was
        decoded and keyed the database with different bytes. If 0.03
        opened your database with such a key, pass the decoded bytes
        instead: MIME::Base64::decode_base64($old_key)
        Stories, stickers and custom emoji, Telegram Stars and gifts,
        and Telegram Business
        Custom emoji, bulk and paid reactions
        on_command and on_callback_data routers, and ask() for
        one-shot questions
        Opt-in retry on 429, off by default
        macOS is now CI tested; the BSDs are unsupported
        star_transactions accepts a chat as its owner, not only a user
        set_default_reaction and message_reactions accept a custom
        emoji, matching react()
        A missing required argument now croaks instead of sending a
        request with a zero id
        INCOMPATIBLE: send_album croaks on wait => 'sent', which it
        could never honour; drop the option
        INCOMPATIBLE: new() croaks on an option it does not know,
        including a misspelled on_* handler. A typo in
        database_encryption_key used to ship the session unencrypted
        INCOMPATIBLE: keepalive() with no argument is a getter. It used
        to turn keepalive back on, so reading the setting re-took the
        loop reference that keepalive(0) had released
        The methods whose last argument is an on/off flag croak on an
        option written in that slot, which used to invert them
        INCOMPATIBLE: a chat, message, user, file, story or topic id
        must now look like a number. A value that only happened to
        numify -- text, or an option name that landed in the slot --
        croaks instead of being sent as a zero. Surrounding space and a
        leading sign are still accepted, so an id read from a file or
        the environment without a chomp still works. api_id is checked
        the same way
        INCOMPATIBLE: an odd option list croaks, so a wrapper that
        forwards an absent callback as undef must omit it instead
        INCOMPATIBLE: set_database_encryption_key encodes its key like
        the constructor option, and needs the same migration
        INCOMPATIBLE: a single-slot on_* handler is removed by a false
        argument. 0.03 ignored one, so a handler could not be removed
        at all; forwarding a handler you may not have now takes away
        the one you had, including one given to new()
        muting a scope no longer disables its notification and story
        sounds
        load_chats takes list, so the archive and folders can be paged
        send and call accept the callback last, as everything else does
        editInlineMessageCaption honours caption_above
        The cached chat positions keep one entry per folder, where
        folders used to overwrite each other, and drop a list the chat
        has left when TDLib sends the full set; chat_lists is kept
        current as the chat joins and leaves lists
        Text methods accept a formattedText, such as translate returns,
        instead of sending it as HASH(0x...); plain-text fields such as
        a bio or a chat description croak on one
        An upload that fails or is cancelled after reporting progress
        releases its on_upload watcher
        INCOMPATIBLE: a setter croaks when its new value is left out,
        rather than clearing what is there: set_password (which switched
        two-step verification off), set_bio, set_username,
        set_chat_description, set_supergroup_username, set_bot_name,
        set_bot_description, set_bot_short_description and the
        set_business_account_* pair. Pass the empty string to clear
        INCOMPATIBLE: on_callback_query and on_callback_data also
        receive presses on messages sent through inline mode, which
        carry inline_message_id and no chat_id, and presses on messages
        sent for a connected business account, which carry
        connection_id. A handler that always reads chat_id now needs to
        check for it
        A login step TDLib refused keeps TDLib's error code, so
        retry_after() reads a login flood wait
        INCOMPATIBLE: on_upload croaks without a callback, as on_command
        does; pass undef to remove a watcher
        delete_messages_by_sender accepts a chat as the sender
        mute and unmute keep a cached chat's own sound and preview
        choices
        join_requests takes offset_request and invite_link_members
        offset_member, so both can be paged past their first page
        send_inline_result honours topic, reply_to, silent and schedule
        INCOMPATIBLE: send_inline_result, forward_messages and
        send_quick_reply croak on wait => 'sent', which none of them
        could honour; drop the option
        Argument errors name the caller's line
        INCOMPATIBLE: set_profile_photo sets the account's main photo.
        It set the public fallback one, which privacy settings show only
        when the main photo is hidden; pass public => 1 for that
        INCOMPATIBLE: a poll lets a voter change or take back a vote
        unless revoting => 0. Every poll refused both; a quiz still does
        INCOMPATIBLE: search_all searches every chat, archived ones
        included, where it searched the main list only. list => 'main'
        or 'archive' narrows it, and a folder id croaks: TDLib cannot
        search a folder
        A plain-text name, title, bio, username or description croaks on
        a formattedText and takes an object that stringifies, such as a
        URI
        load_active_stories reports the end of a story list as success,
        as load_chats does
        post_story calls back at once when TDLib answers with the final
        story, which is how a bot's repost is answered
        set_menu_button puts back the commands list with commands => 1,
        and Telegram's default button when called with neither it nor a
        text
        A folder spec croaks on an unknown key, which TDLib would have
        taken as the flag turned off, and its name may be a formattedText
        chat() and user() accept an id spelled as the rest of the API
        accepts one, with surrounding space or a leading sign
        on_inline_query passes user_location through
        mark_read is one request and no longer opens the chat, which put
        it at the top of the account's recently opened chats and kept it
        loaded in TDLib for the life of the process
        Every caller-supplied text field croaks on a reference instead
        of sending HASH(0x...): names, titles, queries, usernames, invite
        links, sticker set names and keywords, ids, offsets, passwords and
        callback data
        A file argument croaks on a hashref that is not an InputFile,
        which used to be sent as the file itself
        call takes the callback, or its options, in place of the
        argument hashref, for a function that needs no arguments
        The offline test hook _inject_raw is now inject_raw
        INCOMPATIBLE: every number an argument carries -- a limit, an
        offset, a duration, a coordinate, each id in a list -- must look
        like a number. A reference was sent as its memory address, so
        reply_to => $message sent a plain message instead of a reply
        INCOMPATIBLE: a point in time -- schedule, reschedule's $when, a
        ban's until, an emoji status's or invite link's expires, a
        message or search date, an away-message schedule -- croaks on a
        small number. TDLib read one as a date in 1970 and, without an
        error, sent the message at once, made the ban permanent or
        cleared the status
        INCOMPATIBLE: a method that takes no options croaks on an
        argument past its positional ones, including a forwarded undef
        callback; set_chat_title($chat, title => 'New') renamed the
        chat "title"
        A callback written before a method's options croaks instead of
        being dropped
        A flag croaks on a reference that is not an object, including
        \0, which perl reads as true
        login, close and me take the callback last; login(undef, $cb)
        never called back
        A reference as bot_token, phone_number or a register name croaks
        in new() instead of leaving login waiting forever
        INCOMPATIBLE: set_slow_mode, set_auto_delete and
        set_discussion_group croak when the value is left out, which
        cleared the setting; pass 0 to clear
        set_birthdate croaks on a date that does not exist, a month
        counted from 0, a year outside 1800 to 3000, or a partial date,
        each of which TDLib took as clearing the birthdate
        set_greeting_message croaks on inactivity_days other than 7, 14,
        21 or 28, which turned the greeting off
        set_business_location croaks on a latitude without a longitude,
        or the reverse
        download takes on_progress without a main callback
        cancel_download croaks on a callback, which it never called
        post_story, edit_story, the reaction methods, message_count's
        filter, remote_file's file_type and business_features's source
        take an object that stringifies
        A list given where an arrayref belongs croaks at the call site
        instead of dying inside the module
        A retry or timeout setting croaks unless it is a number

0.03    2026-08-27
        Mini Apps, forum topics, chat and group management, folders,
        contacts, payments, secret chats, bot provisioning, and
        schema validated call()

0.02    2026-08-26
        Entity text slicing, unicode documentation, GTK4/Tickit/MCP examples

0.01    2026-08-22
        Initial release: synchronous td_execute binding, EV-integrated
        asynchronous transport, authorization state machine, and
        convenience layers for users, chats, messages and files.
